                <pb facs="0276" n="268" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg268"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.115 Eastern States Petroleum Co./46:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">Then in
                        France</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-01T21:00:00-05:00">February 1, 1938—9
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>B–408. Reference Fisher’s report of 31st through Consulate at Gibraltar. We are
                    assuming that the indication of intention to release ship and crew is true and
                    will be carried out immediately. Please keep in touch with Franco representative
                    and advise us of all developments in this connection. You should also make
                    further urgent representations with a view to effecting immediate release of
                    captain.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
